---
/**
 * The /admin editor shell. This is an Astro route rather than a plain file in
 * public/, because the dev server resolves public/ subfolders only by exact
 * filename — /admin/ would fall through to the 404 page. The CMS bundle and
 * its config stay in public/admin/ and are loaded by absolute path.
 */
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" />
    <title>Atelier Nys — Editor</title>
    <!--
      Leaves Artworks as the only section in the editor. Photos belong to a
      work and are added from inside it, so the asset library — a file browser
      offering the same images again as "All assets" and "Global assets" — is
      only one more thing to wonder about.

      It has to go here: Sveltia has no setting for it. The tab appears
      whenever any media folder is configured (public/admin/config.yml has
      two, the global one and the per-work one), and dropping either would
      break uploads rather than hide the tab.

      Matched on the shortcut and not the label, because the label follows the
      browser's language while Alt+2 is the asset library in every locale — it
      is the only Alt+2 in the bundle. `is:inline` keeps Astro from scoping the
      rule to this file's own markup, which is empty: the CMS builds its
      interface at runtime.
    -->
    <style is:inline>
      [aria-keyshortcuts='Alt+2'] {
        display: none !important;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <script is:inline src="/admin/sveltia-cms.js" type="module"></script>
  </body>
</html>
